Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Most colour advice is a static chart. You\Ndecide you are a winter, buy a foundation, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.61,0:00:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,it is the wrong depth for your actual skin,\Nbecause nothing ever looked at your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.70,0:00:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Chroma starts from the opposite end. It\Nmeasures your face with the YouCam API, then
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.53,0:00:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,computes everything else from those\Nmeasurements.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.61,0:00:24.62,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the deployed app. You give it one\Nphoto. The analysis is a real call to the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.62,0:00:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,YouCam skin tone analysis endpoint. There is a\Nrecorded sample too, labelled as recorded, but
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.24,0:00:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I will run it live.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.65,0:00:36.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I choose the live path, pick a photo, and run\Nthe measurement. The photo goes to the YouCam
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.99,0:00:40.45,Default,,0,0,0,,skin tone analysis API, which returns the\Nmeasured colours.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.71,0:00:46.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Four colours, straight from the API: skin,\Nlips, eyes and brows, each with its measured
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.11,0:00:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,lightness, chroma and hue. Nothing is averaged\Nor filled in. The API did not return hair
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.57,0:00:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,colour, so the app lists it as missing and\Nlowers its confidence, rather than inventing a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.09,0:00:57.99,Default,,0,0,0,,value.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.72,0:01:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,From those four hex values, Chroma derives a\Nseasonal profile. Here, Bright Spring. The app
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.53,0:01:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,shows its work: every signal that voted on the\Nundertone, and what each contributed. This is
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.41,0:01:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,a styling framework, not a medical diagnosis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.54,0:01:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The YouCam makeup engine accepts arbitrary hex\Ncolours, so the looks are not presets. Each is
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.15,0:01:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,computed from the measured palette, and the\Nexact transformation is printed under every
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.40,0:01:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,swatch.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.08,0:01:37.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the try-on. I press render, and the\Ncomputed look is sent to the YouCam makeup
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.30,0:01:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,virtual try-on endpoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.09,0:01:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the composited image: the same photo,\Nwith the look computed from the measured
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.06,0:01:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,colours. Nothing is a preset, and nothing is\Nmanually edited.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.84,0:01:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The same measurement drives the shopping\Nadvice. Any garment colour is scored against
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.65,0:02:02.57,Default,,0,0,0,,the palette with CIEDE2000, the perceptual\Ndistance the makeup engine uses, and the app
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.57,0:02:04.89,Default,,0,0,0,,suggests a colour that would work better.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.15,0:02:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Foundation is matched on depth first,\Nundertone second, because the wrong depth is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.91,0:02:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,far more visible than slightly wrong warmth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.73,0:02:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Measure, interpret, personalize, try on,\Ncompare. One measurement, and every
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.90,0:02:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,recommendation traces back to it. That is the\Nwhole idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.03,0:02:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Try it at chroma-r8sd.vercel.app.
